Enables origin-keyed process isolation for most pages (i.e., those assigned to an origin-keyed agent cluster by default). This improves security but also increases the number of processes created. Note: enabling this feature also enables 'Origin-keyed Agent Clusters by default'.
Collaboration Messaging
Enables the messaging framework within the collaboration feature, including features such as recent activity, dirty dots, and description action chips.
Isolated sandboxed iframes
When enabled, applies process isolation to iframes with the 'sandbox' attribute and without the 'allow-same-origin' permission set on that attribute. This also applies to documents with a similar CSP sandbox header, even in the main frame. The affected sandboxed documents can be grouped into processes based on their URL's site or origin. The default grouping when enabled is per-site.
Omit TLS client certificates if credential mode disallows
Strictly conform the Fetch spec to omit TLS client certificates if credential mode disallows. Without this flag enabled, Chrome will always try sending client certificates regardless of the credential mode.
XSLT
Toggles whether or not XSLT is supported by the browser.
Symphonia Audio Decoding
Enables using the experimental Symphonia audio decoder instead of using FFMPEG for decoding audio.
Permission Module for unused sites in Safety Check
When enabled, adds the unused sites permission module to Safety Check on desktop. The module will be shown depending on the browser state.
Enable Perfetto system tracing
When enabled, Chrome will attempt to connect to the system tracing service
Click-To-Call
Enable the click-to-call feature.
CSS Gamut Mapping
Enable experimental CSS gamut mapping implementation.
Background Resource Fetch
Process resource requests in a background thread inside Blink.
Renderer-side content decoding
Enables renderer-side content decoding (decompression). When enabled, the network service sends compressed HTTP response bodies to the renderer process.
AI Mode Omnibox Entrypoint always navigates
If enabled, clicking aim button in omnibox always navigates directly to google.com/aimode.
Omnibox AI Mode Space Does Not Activate
If enabled, pressing space when the AI mode button has focus will insert a space into the omnibox instead of activating the button.
Dynamic Aim Submit
Enables dynamic aim button submission variants.
WebUI Omnibox AIM Popup
If enabled, using certain trigger operations the omnibox suggestions popup transition to showing the AI-Mode compose-box input and suggestions.
WebUI Omnibox AIM Popup Disable Animation
If enabled, there will no longer be animation in the WebUI Omnibox AIM popup.
WebUI Omnibox Hide AIM URL
If enabled, hides the AIM button when the default suggestion is a URL.
WebUI Omnibox Full Popup
If enabled, shows the omnibox suggestions and the search input in the popup in WebUI.
WebUI Omnibox Full Popup V2
If enabled, then both the input row and suggestions dropdown (in the Omnibox) will be rendered using the WebUI stack (i.e. the cutout for the location bar will be removed). NOTE: This flag is intended to control the next-gen Omnibox experience and will eventually supersede the 'WebUI Omnibox Full Popup' feature flag.
WebUI Omnibox Popup
If enabled, shows the omnibox suggestions in the popup in WebUI.
WebUI Omnibox Popup Debug Mode
Enables the WebUI for omnibox suggestions without modifying the popup UI.
WebUI Omnibox Popup Selection Control
If enabled, the WebUI omnibox popup will control its own selection state.
WebUI Omnibox Simplification
If enabled, the WebUI omnibox popup will have a different UX for the entrypoint to composebox.
Group Promo Prototype
Enables prototype for group promo.
Use DMSAA for tiles
Switches skia to use DMSAA instead of MSAA for tile raster
Sync account settings
Enables syncing account settings to the server.
Sync autofill valuable metadata
Enables syncing valuable metadata for autofill to the server.
Sync wallet flight reservations
Enables syncing flight reservations in the wallet to the server.
Sync wallet vehicle registrations
Enables syncing vehicle registrations in the wallet to the server.
Compression dictionary transport
Enables compression dictionary transport.
Compression dictionary transport ttl
Enables support for the 'ttl' parameter in the 'use-as-dictionary' HTTP response header.
Changes the target playout delay for Cast mirroring.
Choose a target playout delay for Cast mirroring. A lower delay will decrease latency, but may impact other quality indicators.
Enable ProcessPerSite up to main frame threshold
Proactively reuses same-site renderer processes to host multiple main frames, up to a certain threshold.
getDisplayMedia() confers transient activation.
When getDisplay() is invoked by the application, the user is shown a dialog which allows them to share a tab, a window or a screen. If this flag is enabled, then after the user chooses what to share, transient activation is conferred on the Web application.
Glass Frame
Enables a glass effect on the browser frame.
Toolbar Glow Up
Enables the Toolbar Glow Up feature.
Rounded Icons
Enables rounded icons.
Tab Group Color Refresh
Update the color selection for tab groups.
Menu Simplification
Enables the menu simplification feature.
WebUI Refresh 2026
Enables the WebUI Refresh 2026 feature.
Enable RenderDocument
Enable swapping RenderFrameHosts on same-site navigations
Default SiteInstanceGroups
Put sites that don't need isolation in their own SiteInstance in a defaultSiteInstanceGroup (per BrowsingContextGroup) instead of in a default SiteInstance.
CWS Info Fast Check
When enabled, Chrome checks and fetches metadata for installed extensions more frequently.
Extension Disable Unsupported Developer
When enabled, disable unpacked extensions if developer mode is off.
Privacy Sandbox Enrollment Overrides
Allows a list of sites to use Privacy Sandbox features without them being enrolled and attested into the Privacy Sandbox experiment. See: https://developer.chrome.com/en/docs/privacy-sandbox/enroll/
Enable prefetching of risk data during payments autofill retrieval
When enabled, risk data is prefetched during payments autofill flows to reduce user-perceived latency.
Dynamic Profile Country
When enabled, Chrome updates the country associated with the profile on open
Enable generic OIDC profile management
Enables profile management triggered by generic OIDC authentications.
Desktop PWA Link Capturing
Enables opening links from Chrome in an installed PWA. Currently under reimplementation.
Protected Audiences Consented Debug Token
Enables Protected Audience Consented Debugging with the provided token. Protected Audience auctions running on a Bidding and Auction API trusted server with a matching token will be able to log information about the auction to enable debugging. Note that this logging may include information about the user's browsing history normally kept private.
Deprecate the unload event
Controls the default for Permissions-Policy unload. If enabled, unload handlers are deprecated and will not receive the unload event unless a Permissions-Policy to enable them has been explicitly set. If  disabled, unload handlers will continue to receive the unload event unless explicitly disabled by Permissions-Policy, even during the gradual rollout of their deprecation.
Enable risk-based authentication for FPAN retrieval
When enabled, server card retrieval will begin with a risk-based check instead of jumping straight to CVC or biometric auth.
Ack CopyOutputRequest early for View Transition
If enabled, send acks for CopyOutputRequest completion immediately to unblock navigation for ViewTransitions while CopyOutputRequests are in progress. This is a fast-path for ViewTransitions.
Mac PWA notification attribution
Route notifications for PWAs on Mac through the app shim, attributing notifications to the correct apps.
Use Ad-hoc Signing for Web App Shims
Ad-hoc code signing ensures that each PWA app shim has a unique identity. This allows macOS subsystems to correctly distinguish between multiple PWAs.
Profiles Reordering
Enables profiles reordering in the Profile Picker main view by drag and dropping the Profile Tiles. The order is saved when changed and persisted.
Device Bound Session Credentials
Enables Google session credentials binding to cryptographic keys.
Device Bound Session Credentials with software keys
Enables mock software-backed cryptographic keys for Google session credentials binding and Chrome refresh tokens binding (not secure). This is intended to be used for manual testing only.
Compose Selection Nudge
Enables nudge on selection for Compose
Show permission grants from Related Website Sets
Shows permission grants created by Related Website Sets in Chrome Settings UI and Page Info Bubble, default is hidden
Save Password Contextual UI
Improved page action indicator and dialog UI when the user has blocklisted the current site for password saving.
Enable Isolated Web Apps to bypass USB restrictions
When enabled, allows Isolated Web Apps to access blocklisted devices and protected interfaces through WebUSB API.
Enable 3DS authentication for virtual cards
When enabled, Chrome will trigger 3DS authentication during a virtual card retrieval if a challenge is required, 3DS authentication is available for the card, and FIDO is not.
Send Tab To Self enhanced handoff
Enables an enhanced version of Send Tab To Self that propagates more information, such as form fields and scroll position.
Enable data sharing debug logs
Enables the data sharing infrastructure to log and save debug messages that can be shown in the internals page.
data-sharing-debug-logs
Device Bound Session Credentials (Standard)
Enables the official version of Device Bound Session Credentials. For more information see https://github.com/WICG/dbsc.
Device Bound Session Credentials (Standard) Persistence
Enables session persistence for the official version of Device Bound Session Credentials.
Device Bound Session Credentials (Standard) - Federated Registrations
Enables federated session registration for the official version of Device Bound Session Credentials.
Device Bound Session Credentials (Standard) DevTools Debugging
Enables DevTools debugging for the official version of Device Bound Session Credentials.
Device Bound Session Credentials (Standard) on Google
Enables Device Bound Session Credentials (Standard) to register sessions on Google sites
Experiment ID for Device Bound Session Credentials (Standard) on Google
Sets the experiment ID sent when Device Bound Session Credentials (Standard) registers sessions on Google sites
Responsive Iframes
Enable responsively-sized iframes.
Replace all sync-related UI with sign-in ones
When enabled, all sync-related UIs will be replaced by sign-in ones.
Replace sync promos with sign-in promos (New Sign-in events)
When enabled, all sync-related UIs will be replaced by sign-in ones. Similar to #replace-sync-promos-with-sign-in-promos-desktop but only enables extensions and bookmarks sync on new signin events.
Uno phase 2 follow-up
UI tweaks for signin surfaces
Showing password suggestions on autofocused password forms
Enables showing password suggestions without requiring the user to click on the already focused field if the field was autofocused on the page load.
In-flow resolution of errors during password saving
Starts the password manager error resolution flow after offering to save a password.
Enable optimization guide dogfood logging
If this client is a Google-internal dogfood client, overrides enterprise policy to enable model quality logs. Googlers: See go/chrome-mqls-debug-logging for details.
Use passkey from another device in the context menu
Hides the "Use a passkey" entry from the autofill popup for conditional WebAuthn requests. Moves the entry point to the context menu.
Prompt API for Gemini Nano
Enables the exploratory Prompt API, allowing you to send natural language instructions to a built-in large language model (Gemini Nano in Chrome). Exploratory APIs are designed for local prototyping to help discover potential use cases, and may never launch. These explorations will inform the built-in AI roadmap [1]. This API is primarily intended for natural language processing tasks such as summarizing, classifying, or rephrasing text. It is NOT suitable for use cases that require factual accuracy (e.g. answering knowledge questions). You must comply with our Prohibited Use Policy [2] which provides additional details about appropriate use of Generative AI.
Prompt API for Gemini Nano with Multimodal Input
Extends the exploratory Prompt API with image and audio input types. Allows you to supplement natural language instructions for a built-in large language model (Gemini Nano in Chrome) with image and audio inputs. Exploratory APIs are designed for local prototyping to help discover potential use cases, and may never launch. These explorations will inform the built-in AI roadmap [1]. This API enhancement is primarily intended for natural language processing tasks associated with visual and auditory data, such as generating rough descriptions of pictures and sounds. It is NOT suitable for use cases that require factual accuracy (e.g. answering knowledge questions). You must comply with our Prohibited Use Policy [2] which provides additional details about appropriate use of Generative AI.
Writer API for Gemini Nano
Enables the Writer API, allowing you to write a piece of text with a built-in large language model (Gemini Nano in Chrome).The API may be subject to changes including the supported options.Please refer to the built-in AI article [1] for details. You must comply with our Prohibited Use Policy [2] which provides additional details about appropriate use of Generative AI.
Rewriter API for Gemini Nano
Enables the Rewriter API, allowing you to rewrite a piece of text with a built-in large language model (Gemini Nano in Chrome).The API may be subject to changes including the supported options.Please refer to the built-in AI article [1] for details. You must comply with our Prohibited Use Policy [2] which provides additional details about appropriate use of Generative AI.
Proofreader API for Gemini Nano
Enables the Proofreader API, allowing you to proofread a piece of textwith a built-in large language model (Gemini Nano in Chrome).The API may be subject to changes including the supported options.Please refer to the built-in AI article [1] for details. You must comply with our Prohibited Use Policy [2] which provides additional details about appropriate use of Generative AI.
Classifier API for Tiny Model
Enables the Classifier API, allowing you to classify a piece of text with a built-in tiny model in Chrome. The API may be subject to changes including the supported options. Please refer to the built-in AI article [1] for details. You must comply with our Prohibited Use Policy [2] which provides additional details about appropriate use of Generative AI.
Gemma 4 for Built-in AI
Enables all built-in AI APIs (Prompt, Summarizer, Writer, etc.) with the Gemma 4 model.
Summarizer API with Performance Preference
Adds the "preference" create option to the Summarizer API. Allows the developer to choose between "capability", "speed", and "auto" to hint at the desired balance between performance and capability. We're rapidly iterating on the training set for the smaller expert model used with the 'speed' preference, and welcome your feedback here: https://issues.chromium.org/issues/new?component=1617227
Summarizer API for Gemini Nano
Enables the Summarizer API, allowing you to summarize a piece of text with a built-in large language model (Gemini Nano in Chrome). The API may be subject to changes including the supported options. Please refer to the built-in AI article [1] for details. You must comply with our Prohibited Use Policy [2] which provides additional details about appropriate use of Generative AI.
On-device category classifier
Enables the on-device category classifier.
LiteRT-LM for On-Device AI
Use LiteRT-LM runtime for on-device model service inference.
CSS Grid Lanes Layout
Enable experimental CSS Grid Lanes Layout implementation. Simple layouts with grid-lanes are supported. Subgrid and fragmentation are not supported yet. The syntax to use CSS Grid Lanes is `display: grid-lanes` together with grid properties (i.e. `grid-column`, `grid-row`, etc.). More details on grid-lanes syntax can be found at https://www.w3.org/TR/css-grid-3/#masonry-model.
Hibernation for 2D canvas
Enables canvas hibernation for 2D canvas.
Visited URL ranking deduplication strategy
Enables visited url ranking service to use one of various deduplication strategies.
Enable visited URL aggregates visibility score based filtering
Enables filtering of visited URL aggregates based on history URL visibility scores.
Infinite Tabs Freezing
Freezes eligible tabs which are not in the 5 most recently used ones, to preserve Chrome speed as new tabs are created. Tabs providing background functionality (e.g. playing audio, handling a video call) are not eligible for freezing.
Memory Purge on Freeze Limit
Do not purge memory in renderers with frozen pages more than once per backgrounded interval, to minimize overhead when pages are periodically unfrozen. To be enabled with memory-purge-on-freeze-limit.
Translate Open Settings
Add an option to the translate bubble menu to open language settings.
Lens AIM M3 Side Panel Suggestions
Enables suggestions in the Lens composebox. This will have an effect only when the Lens search AIM M3 flag is also enabled.
Lens AIM M3 Side Panel Suggestions Gradient Background
Enables a gradient background for the Lens composebox dropdown that does not cover the entire side panel.
Data Controls drag-and-drop enforcement
Enables Data Controls drag-and-drop enforcement.
Data Controls enforcement for search context menu item
Enables the Enterprise Data Controls for restricting data exfiltration with the "Search with..." context menu item.
Data Sharing
Enabled all Data Sharing related UI and features.
Collaboration Entreprise V2
Enables the collaboration feature for entreprise users within the same domain.
Shared Tab Group messaging sync
Enable the messaging sync backend for shared tab groups.
Data Sharing Join Only
Enabled Data Sharing Joining flow related UI and features.
Data Sharing server environment
Sets data sharing server environment.
Data Sharing Versioning Test Scenarios
Testing multiple scenarios for versioning.
History Sync Alternative Illustration
Enables history sync alternative illustration.
Enable JavaScript live editing in DevTools
Re-enable the deprecated feature in DevTools' Sources panel to apply code edits to the target page live.
PermissionsAIv4
Use the Permission Predictions Service and the AIv4 model to surface permission notification requests using a quieter UI when the likelihood of the user granting the permission is predicted to be low. Requires `Make Searches and Browsing Better` to be enabled.
PermissionsAIP92
Use the Permission Predictions Service and with P92 adjustments to surface permission notification requests using a quieter UI when the likelihood of the user granting the permission is predicted to be low. Requires `Make Searches and Browsing Better` to be enabled.
Permissions Gesture Gated Prompts
Mute non-user-initiated permission requests.
Lens overlay translate button
Enables translate button via the Lens overlay.
Lens overlay latency optimizations
Enables latency optimizations for the Lens overlay.
Lens overlay image context menu actions
Enables image context menu actions in the Lens overlay.
Lens overlay updated visuals
Enables updated visuals in the Lens selection overlay.
Enables AIM in Lens side panel.
Enables AIM follow ups with the Lens overlay results side panel.
Lens Side Panel Unification
Unifies the Lens and Contextual Tasks side panels into a single panel.
Segmentation survey internals page and model
Enable internals page for survey and fetching model
Enable buy now pay later on Autofill
When enabled, users will have the option to pay with buy now pay later on specific merchant webpages.
Enable syncing buy now pay later user data.
When enabled, Chrome will sync user data related to buy now pay later.
Enable CVC storage and filling standalone form enhancement for payments autofill
When enabled, this will enhance the CVV storage project. The enhancement will enable CVV storage suggestions for standalone CVC fields.
Enable retrieval of card info(with CVC) from issuer for enrolled cards
When enabled, runtime retrieval of CVC along with card number and expiry from issuer for enrolled cards will be enabled during form fill.
Translation API streaming split by sentence
Enables sentence-split streaming for on-device translation API.
Grouped affiliation password suggestions
Enables offering credentials coming from grouped domains for filling
Contextual cueing
Enables the contextual cueing system to support showing actions.
Contextual cueing V2
Enables the contextual cueing system version 2.
PartitionAlloc with Advanced Checks
Enables an extra security layer on PartitionAlloc.
Partition the Visited Link Database, including 'self-links'
Style links as visited only if they have been clicked from this top-level site and frame origin before. Additionally, style links pointing to the same URL as the page it is displayed on, which have been :visited from any top-level site and frame origin, if they are displayed in a top-level frame or same-origin subframe.
Predictable Reported Quota
Enables reporting of a predictable quota from the StorageManager's estimate API. This flag is intended only for validating if this change caused an unforeseen bug.
BookmarkBarPrefetch
If enabled, bookmarkbar can trigger prefetch
NewTabPagePrefetch
If enabled, NewTabPage can trigger prefetch
Mac A11y API Migration
Enables the migration to the new Cocoa accessibility API.
More Lens overlay translate languages
Enables more translate languages in the Lens Overlay.
